Book Revision

To search for a key, start current at head and traverse the list while current != null. At each node, compare current.val with key. If they are equal, return true; otherwise move to the next node using current = current.next. If current becomes null, the key is not present, so return false.

Time: O(n)
Auxiliary Space: O(1)

code
================================

/*
Definition of ListNode

class ListNode {
    int val;              // Stores the value of the current node
    ListNode next;        // Stores the reference to the next node

    ListNode(int value) { // Constructor to create a node
        this.val = value; // Store the given value in the node
        this.next = null; // Initially, this node points to nothing
    }
}
*/

class Solution {

    public boolean searchKey(ListNode head, int key) {

        // Start traversal from the first node (head)
        ListNode current = head;

        // Continue traversing while current points to a node
        while (current != null) {

            // Check whether the current node's value equals the key
            if (current.val == key) {

                // Key is found, so return true immediately
                return true;
            }

            // Move current to the next node
            current = current.next;
        }

        // We reached the end without finding the key
        return false;
    }
}
